Z||000006||Philphine||06-23-2001||08:53 PM||||don't know if you have a 4 or 6 cyl. or what you've done already. just looked at mine and some of the cheaper things were just style stuff (or lack thereof depending on whos judging). a couple of the cheaper ones were;<P>painted my front speaker grills black to better match the dash. i thought they looked like patches before. <P>put in front hood scoops. they cost me about $30 and hardware was about another $10-15. guess that will depend on what you find. i also got another hood to try it on, that cost can be saved depending on how brave you are.<P>if it's a 4cyl a nice exhaust tip. also if it's a four maybe hit the junkyards or find someone whos upgrading and switch to dual exhaust. i got a brand new stock gt exhaust for my 4cyl. for about $160 installed. if you can find a nice used one maybe you can get it cheap enough to where installation won't hurt too much.<P>fool around with making a side scoop. i made a fairly ugly one for about $15, but it had that "did it myself" factor and i used it till i got some more. 2 or 3 people have shown doable designs.<P>keep the compatible car wheel list handy if you need (or just want different) wheels cause you never know what might pop up. i have most of a set of cavalier z24 wheels i got from a guy who didn't know what they were. he was told they were for a chevy and he tried to put them on his blazer. got 3 for $75. i'll get a 4th one when i see one cheap.    <P>got a wing or want one? check the old threads to see what people have subbed for stock wings. i have a couple of different mustang wings i like and they're much more common and cheaper to come by, as are camaro/firebird wings. just set it on your car and see if you like it and if it will mount well.<P>i guess a lot of that will depend on what you luck across and/or what you have already or are after. ||||reg||1
